# CoW true-lazy P3 tier-1 — match-arm-NESTED mutation witness.
#
# Same shape as cow_p3_cond_nested_mutate but the source mutation
# (`coll.fill(...)`, a realloc) is buried inside a `match` arm. The
# construct-agnostic forward-scan recurses through match arms too, so
# `coll` is marked mutated and the `String x = coll.get(0).unwrap()` bind
# does NOT flip — `x` eager-clones, and the post-`match` reads observe the
# pre-mutation value. Soundness over flow-precision: tier-1 declines the
# flip whenever ANY mutation of the source exists anywhere in the function.
void main():
    Vector[String] coll = ["alphalonglonglongstring", "betalonglonglongstring"]
    String x = coll.get(0).unwrap()
    int sel = 1
    match sel:
        case 0:
            print("noop")
        else:
            coll.fill(4, "z")
            coll.fill(4, "newlonglonglonglonglonglonglonglongstringhere")
    print(x)
    print(x.len())
